   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1
National and Sub national institutions and communities have improved capacities to prevent and address violent extremism.

1.1 - # of Local action plans (aligned to National PCVE Strategy) developed
1.2 - # of priority activities implemented at the targeted governorate 
1.3 - # of men and women supported with opportunities to increase resilience to violent extremism e.g.: 
- Economic empowerment/skills building.
-Mental health and psycho-social support.
-Early warning response and alternative narratives
-Participation in policy/planning/budgeting or other decision-making process.
1.4 - # of CSOs trained and engaged in PVE activities of which at least 5% are CSOs led by women

Output 2 
Families perceived to be affiliated with ISIL, are successfully reintegrated into communities that are more resilient to violent extremism.

2.1 - # of assessments carried out
2.2 - # Women specific activities to enhance PVE at the community level implemented
2.3 - # of Returned families reintegrated (disaggregated location)
2.4 - # of LPCs and local structures supported to facilitate reintegration of returnees</narrative>
    </description>
